+
+Executed the predeclared cost-sensitivity check for the short-horizon momentum
+candidate (lookback 3/5/10) on the collected universe with the repository's
+existing realistic cost model and a matched coin-flip null. New infrastructure:
+`research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`,
+`research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`, and
+`tests/test_momentum_cost.py` (12 focused unit tests).
+
+Method: dataset `yf-ohlcv-universe-2009-to-2026-10-03`; cost grid `zero` /
+`realistic` ($2/trade, $0.003/share, 2c fixed + 5 bps proportional — copied from
+`examples/ma_crossover_real_data.py` and `examples/volatility_regime_filter.py`) /
+`stress2x` (exactly 2x every cost parameter); walk-forward per segment
+train=252d/test=84d/warmup=60d/overlap=60d; 4 contiguous volatility blocks; min
+400 bars/segment; each (lookback, cost level) candidate vs a matched coin-flip null
+run under the SAME `cfg` so both pay the same costs.
+
+DECISIVE FINDING — the tested "momentum" signal is not momentum.
+`research/backtest/regime_stability.py::momentum_signals` (and
+`mean_reversion_signals`) compute `np.mean(np.log(closes[i-lookback+1:i+1]))` —
+the MEAN LOG PRICE over the window — not the previous-N-day return
+`log(close[i]) - log(close[i-lookback])`. For every collected ticker (prices > $1)
+the mean log price is positive on ~every bar, so the momentum weight is +1 on
+4460/4465 bars with ONE position flip (dominant weight share 1.000). Independent
+recomputation shows the signal's sign agrees with the TRUE previous-5-day return
+sign on only 0.538–0.580 of bars (near coin-flip); NVDA is 0.585 dominant / 2 flips
+only because its split-adjusted price dipped below $1. The check's signal-validity
+gate (required agreement >= 0.95) fails for all 10 assets, so the primary question
+is recorded `UNVERIFIED_INVALID_SUBJECT`.
+
+Consequences:
+- The cost grid itself was evaluated and independently verified (all gates MATCH),
+  but its subject is a near-constant long (directional beta), not momentum.
+- Cost drag on the candidate is ~0 (a constant position has minimal signal-driven
+  turnover; the +553% AMZN buy-and-hold drift dwarfs costs). The matched iid
+  {-1,0,+1} null turns over on ~2/3 of bars and pays more cost, so its median falls
+  and the candidate-minus-null gap WIDENS under cost (AMZN +0.078 -> +0.085 ->
+  +0.092 at zero/realistic/2x). That is the signature of a directional-beta
+  artifact, not a cost-robust momentum edge.
+- The same defect invalidates the reversal FALSIFIED result (37263008074; the
+  reversal signal is a constant short) and the momentum admission/qualifications
+  (37318950814, 37361000967, 37394344201, `momentum_horizon_gap_analysis`) as
+  evidence about momentum/reversal. The MA-crossover, breakout, cross-sectional
+  relative-strength, and cross-sectional-momentum classes are unaffected (they
+  compute returns/ranks correctly).
+- The earlier "momentum P&L vs reversal P&L correlation -0.99" corroboration is
+  itself a symptom: always-long vs always-short on the same folds must be ~-1.
+
+Mechanical cost classification (reported for completeness, NOT interpretable as
+momentum cost robustness): realistic SURVIVES=5 (AAPL, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA),
+ERODED=1 (MSFT), NO_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM); stress2x SURVIVES=4, ERODED=2
+(adds TSLA), NO_EDGE=4. Per-lookback positive-edge counts (lookback 3/5/10): zero
+6/6/5, realistic 6/6/6, stress2x 5/5/6.
+
+Verification: manifest 10/10 OK; preflight PASSED; leakage PASS on AMZN/JPM with
+the realistic-cost fill-equity audit; zero-cost column cross-consistency vs
+`momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json` MATCH (all 10 tickers x 3 lookbacks);
+independent verifier (5 gates: fresh cost recomputation, independent
+signal-validity recomputation, zero-cost cross-consistency, classification
+reproducibility, determinism) MATCH; determinism identical; 180/180 regression
+tests pass (168 baseline + 12 new).
+
+Decision: VERIFIED_NEGATIVE_RESULT (the cost question is not adjudicable because
+the subject is mis-implemented; the negative/invalidating finding is verified).
+Process decision: IMPROVE — the gate stack needs a signal-construction validity
+gate before any signal class is admitted (a near-constant directional bet passed
+five prior activations and their independent verifiers as "momentum").
+
+Next (single bounded action): fix `momentum_signals`/`mean_reversion_signals` to
+use the previous-N-day log return, add a sign-agreement unit test, and re-run the
+momentum evidence chain (lookback 3/5/10 through the cost grid) before any cost
+conclusion is drawn.
+
